Title: Judge's X Word Puzzle No. 18
Author: Catherine MacMillan
Date: 1927-08-27
Byline: Submitted by Catherine MacMillan, Chicago, Ill. Judge pays $1 for eazh puzzle printed
Source: https://archive.org/details/sim_judge_1927-08-27_93/page/n31/mode/1up
Puzzle-Number: 18
Solution-Source: https://archive.org/details/sim_judge_1927-09-03_93/page/n28/mode/1up


DOCTORS#USHERED
I#ROMAN#NOOSE#E
AMERICA#TONSILS
MAT#TERMITE#SEE
ORAL#SEEDY#TSAR
NINES#SAY#JOUST
DESPOT#N#VALETS
###RAINDROPS###
STROKE#E#WATERS
CHESS#ERG#NOVEL
RELY#ALEUT#YALE
ARE#KIDDERS#DIE
TEATIME#SEASICK
C#SANER#TAKEN#E
HEEDERS#STINGER


A1. What people enjoy poor health? ~ DOCTORS
A7. What did the rejected suitors do at the wedding? ~ USHERED
A13. What was Marcus Aurelius? ~ ROMAN
A14. What was used in old western necking parties? ~ NOOSE
A15. Name something that never seems to dry up. ~ AMERICA
A17. What gets sore when the weather is bad? (plural). ~ TONSILS
A19. Upon what is many a controversy settled? ~ MAT
A20. Name a kind of white ant. ~ TERMITE
A22. What is it that lovers never do in the dark? ~ SEE
A23. What kind of gifts have Congress and women? ~ ORAL
A25. How does the well-dressed man look after he marries? ~ SEEDY
A26. What big gun in Russia is now obsolete? ~ TSAR
A27. What are always going batty? ~ NINES
A29. Name an impolite salutation. ~ SAY
A30. At what medieval debate did the knights often get the point? ~ JOUST
A31. What do clinging vines grow into? ~ DESPOT
A33. What people are judged by their service? (plural). ~ VALETS
A34. What caused the Mississippi flood? ~ RAINDROPS
A35. Name something that has a paralyzing effect. ~ STROKE
A38. What is the easiest thing to take at Saratoga? ~ WATERS
A42. In what game do kings, queens, knights and bishops meet? ~ CHESS
A43. What is the unit of work called? ~ ERG
A45. What is always fictitious? ~ NOVEL
A46. What must you do to have confidence? ~ RELY
A47. What would you call an Eskimo from the Aleutian Islands? ~ ALEUT
A49. At what eastern college did they use to play football? ~ YALE
A50. What does a cockney call a rabbit? ~ ARE
A51. What are "practical jokers"? (plural). ~ KIDDERS
A53. What do chickens do if they're slow in getting across the street? ~ DIE
A54. What is 4 P. M. in England? ~ TEATIME
A56. What do many people get outside of the 12-mile limit? ~ SEASICK
A58. How do most people feel the morning after? ~ SANER
A59. How would you find a desirable apartment for $50 a month? ~ TAKEN
A60. What people sit up and take notice? ~ HEEDERS
A61. What is a mosquito? ~ STINGER

D1. What is the mark of success to most girls? ~ DIAMOND
D2. What are brunettes who live on the Island of Crete called? ~ CRETANS
D3. What is a bleak, rocky hill called? ~ TOR
D4. What should the editor do to an old joke? ~ OMIT
D5. For what are Indianapolis, Louisville and Saratoga noted? ~ RACES
D6. In what are many wise old birds caught? ~ SNARES
D7. How does the little woman find her home after she has been away? ~ UNTIDY
D8. How do people come from Pittsburgh? ~ SOOTY
D9. Name one way of getting an edge on. ~ HONE
D10. What suffix is used to form feminine nouns? ~ ESS
D11. What do publishers do when they're sold out? ~ REISSUE
D12. What are the only really dry places? (plural). ~ DESERTS
D16. Name a queenly person. ~ MARIE
D18. Name an adjective that means "smallest." ~ LEAST
D21. How did our ancestors walk through lovers' lane? ~ MEANDERED
D24. For what disease are people sent to the Island of Molokai? ~ LEPROSY
D26. Name a Russian novelist. ~ TOLSTOY
D28. What people do their best to down liquor? ~ SOAKS
D30. Name of varnishlike liquid made of shellac. ~ JAPAN
D32. What is always hanging around a matinée idol's neck? ~ TIE
D33. What do many take—and few keep? ~ VOW
D35. What would you do in a ticklish situation? ~ SCRATCH
D36. What is opposite here? ~ THERE
D37. What could some married people like for a wedding anniversary present? ~ RELEASE
D39. What are bachelors good at? ~ EVADING
D40. What is "a remaining fragment?" ~ RELIC
D41. What are drug-store cowboys? (comparative degree.) ~ SLEEKER
D43. Who always knocks the younger generation? ~ ELDERS
D44. Who are always being entertained? ~ GUESTS
D47. What must a marksman be? ~ AIMER
D48. What would vertical 28 consider a highball? ~ TREAT
D51. What are poetical cows called? ~ KINE
D52. Name a South American monkey. ~ SAKI
D55. What kind of a pole do frogs spring from? ~ TAD
D57. Name a Japanese coin. ~ SEN


Misprints, kept as printed (printed → meant):
A53: What do chickens do if they're slow in getting across the street? → they're
byline: → each

